UID:OwPKkAVnua
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 180 mins (3h00m)\n\nA crew of professional shoplifte
 rs take aim at a cutthroat fashion maven. It’s like community service.Di
 rector Boots Riley scheduled to attend. Film + Party Tickets: $75 ($55 SI
 FF Members)Film Only Tickets: $40 ($35 SIFF Members)\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/festival/i-love-boosters\n\nEstimated start: 19:10
LOCATION:Paramount Theatre\, 911 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Case 137
DTSTART:20260508T193000Z
DTEND:20260508T214000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T193000Z
UID:38jSgRffAV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nWhen a 20-year-old protester is 
 shot in the head by the police\, wholly unprovoked\, during demonstrations
  in Paris\, it’s up to Stéphanie\, a dedicated officer in the internal 
 affairs unit\, to deliver justice.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/case-1
 37\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 1 (Mon 11 May\, 8:45 PM)\n\nEst
 imated start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Hold a Mountain
DTSTART:20260508T193000Z
DTEND:20260508T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T193000Z
UID:pCtZg9CKrt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nSemi-nomadic shepherd and cheese
 maker Gara raises her 13-year-old niece Nada as her own. As she fights to 
 protect her grazing land from a NATO military expansion\, Nada begins to i
 magine her own future. This film is generously sponsored by Mary Rainwater
 .\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-hold-a-mountain\n\nAlso playing at:\
 n  • PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center (Fri 15 May\, 6:00 PM
 )\n\nEstimated start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Promised Sky
DTSTART:20260508T200000Z
DTEND:20260508T214500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T200000Z
UID:n72G6QR9C2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nA community of Ivorian women navi
 gating the complexities of migrant life in Tunisia are forced to make diff
 icult decisions when they rescue an orphaned girl from a shipwreck.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/promised-sky\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown 
 House 1 (Wed 13 May\, 9:15 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 13:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tell Everyone
DTSTART:20260508T201500Z
DTEND:20260508T222000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T201500Z
UID:isKNh6CGdv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nOn a remote island where trouble
 some women are sent to be forgotten\, an emotionally charged struggle for 
 liberation unfolds in a dazzlingly beautiful and deeply moving historical 
 drama.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/tell-everyone\n\nAlso playing at:\
 n  • Uptown House 2 (Tue 12 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 13:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renoir
DTSTART:20260508T220000Z
DTEND:20260509T001000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T220000Z
UID:diDYt0iwNb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA coming-of-age story following 
 a tomboyish 11-year-old girl whose intellectual father is dying of cancer 
 and mother at her wits’ end. The courageous girl seeks adventures\, some
  involving the paranormal.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/renoir\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • Uptown House 1 (Tue 12 May\, 9:00 PM)\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 15:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Barbara Forever
DTSTART:20260508T223000Z
DTEND:20260509T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T223000Z
UID:IIM0mGQn3M
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nFor five decades\, avant-garde f
 eminist filmmaker Barbara Hammer created groundbreaking lesbian cinema—e
 xploring identity\, gender\, and sexuality\, uncovering erased histories\,
  and putting lesbian lives boldly\, joyfully\, and unapologetically on scr
 een.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/barbara-forever\n\nAlso playing at:\
 n  • Uptown House 3 (Mon 11 May\, 9:00 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 15:40
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drunken Noodles
DTSTART:20260508T223000Z
DTEND:20260509T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T223000Z
UID:YBhjnAyBus
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nNarrative shifts\, flashbacks\, f
 olds\, and even a dash of magical realism mark this quiet examination of m
 odern queer relationships\, presenting three facets of the romantic life o
 f a young New Yorker. This film is generously sponsored by Noel Caraig.\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/drunken-noodles\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • 
 Uptown House 3 (Sun 10 May\, 8:45 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 15:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Franz
DTSTART:20260508T223000Z
DTEND:20260509T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T223000Z
UID:bCDEYHqguG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 127 mins (2h07m)\n\nHow do you make sense of Franz K
 afka? With fictional interviews with Kafka’s friends and family and thri
 lling plunges into his fiction\, Franz does not explain\, but playfully an
 d inventively explores the man and his work.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/franz\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Sun 10 May\, 5:00 PM)\n\nEs
 timated start: 15:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deadline
DTSTART:20260508T230000Z
DTEND:20260509T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T230000Z
UID:CGngD1ZH9f
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nIn Kiwi Chow’s drama-thriller\
 , an elite academy drives students to pills\, rebellion\, and a suicide ul
 timatum—exposing an authority-soaked system through stunning visuals and
  standout young performances. Producer Peiyi Lin scheduled to attend.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/festival/deadline\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown Ho
 use 1 (Sun 10 May\, 8:15 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
