DTSTART:20260509T010000Z
DTEND:20260509T023500Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T010000Z
UID:m1pFCiIZxO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLebanese journalist Janay Boulos 
 and Syrian activist and cameraman Abd Alkader Habak share their extraordin
 ary love story\, told through 13 years of personal archives spanning revol
 utions\, war\, and exile. Director Janay Boulos scheduled to attend. This 
 film is generously sponsored by Katherine & David De Bruyn.\n\nhttps://www
 .siff.net/festival/birds-of-war\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 1 
 (Sat 9 May\, 12:15 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 18:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nuisance Bear
DTSTART:20260509T010000Z
DTEND:20260509T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T010000Z
UID:YWhRl5AEI4
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nA polar bear is forced to navigat
 e a human world of tourists\, wildlife officers\, and hunters as its ancie
 nt migration collides with modern life. When a sacred predator is branded 
 a nuisance\, it becomes unclear who truly belongs in this shared landscape
 . Editor Jocelyne Chaput and Cinematographer Ian Kerr scheduled to attend.
  This film is generously sponsored by Michael Weidemann.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/nuisance-bear\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Sat 9 M
 ay\, 12:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 18:10
LOCATION:PACCAR IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center\, None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shape of Momo
DTSTART:20260509T010000Z
DTEND:20260509T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T010000Z
UID:rB8YMahSoB
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nAfter quitting her job in Delhi\
 , Bishnu returns to her Himalayan village\, only to find the women around 
 her still bound by the same expectations. Change\, it turns out\, is harde
 r than she thought.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/shape-of-momo\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • Film Center (Sun 10 May\, 3:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start:
  18:10
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edie Arnold is a Loser
DTSTART:20260509T013000Z
DTEND:20260509T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T013000Z
UID:hGhsOnDYQJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nLace up your combat boots and whi
 p out that black eyeliner for Edie Arnold is a Loser\, an infectiously cha
 rming coming-of-age flick about a self-proclaimed loser starting a punk ba
 nd at her Catholic high school. Directors Kade Atwood and Megan Rico sched
 uled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/edie-arnold-is-a-loser\n\
 nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 2 (Sat 9 May\, 12:45 PM)\n\nEstimate
 d start: 18:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Power Ballad
DTSTART:20260509T014500Z
DTEND:20260509T033500Z
DTSTAMP:20260509T014500Z
UID:SiuutVN2BL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nWhen Rick (Paul Rudd)\, a past-hi
 s-prime wedding singer\, meets fading boy-band star Danny (Nick Jonas) dur
 ing a gig\, the two bond over music and a late-night jam session. But when
  Danny turns one of Rick's songs into the hit that reignites his career\, 
 Rick sets out to reclaim the recognition he believes he deserves—even if
  it means risking everything he cares about. From writer-director John Car
 ney (Sing Street\, Once)\, Power Ballad is a feel-good story about music\,
  self-respect\, friendship\, and the price of ambition.\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/festival/power-ballad\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Sat 9 May
 \, 3:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 18:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
